Under 15 USC 6801, financial institutions, which include Furnishers of information to credit agencies, are mandated to respect customer privacy and protect the confidentiality of nonpublic personal information. This obligation is critical in safeguarding consumer privacy. 

According to 15 USC 1681 section 604 a section 2, consumer reporting agencies may furnish consumer reports only in accordance with the written instructions of the consumer. Neither XXXX, XXXX, nor any Furnisher of information to credit agencies has obtained my written consent to furnish this information, nor do they possess my consent in any form, be it verbal, non-verbal, implied, or otherwise. 
