As per 15 USC 1681C ( a ) ( 5 ), consumer reporting agencies are prohibited from including adverse items of information in a consumer report without authorization. The account in question is being reported as an adverse item without my permission, a clear violation of this statute. 


XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ) ( XXXX XXXX XXXX ) TransUnion XXXX XXXX Account number : XXXX XXXX XXXX Account type : Credit Credit Credit Account Type : Revolving Revolving Revolving 15 U.S. Code 1681s2 ( A ) ( 1 ) A further stipulates that information should not be furnished if it is known or reasonably believed to be inaccurate. I assert that the information being furnished is inaccurate, and it is the responsibility of XXXX, XXXX, and all Furnishers of information to credit agencies to ensure the accuracy of the data they provide. 

Lastly, 15 U.S. Code 1681e requires consumer reporting agencies to maintain reasonable procedures to avoid violations of the FCRA. It is evident that these reasonable procedures are not being maintained by XXXX, XXXX, or any Furnisher of information to credit agencies. 

Additionally, 12 CFR 1016.7 reaffirms my right to opt out of reporting services at any time. I am hereby exercising this right to opt out of the reporting services provided by XXXX, XXXX, and all Furnishers of information to credit agencies. 

