2. Reporting of Late Payments : I have discovered that XXXX, Equifax and XXXX has reported late payments on my credit report, which is a clear violation of 15 USC 1666B. The FCRA requires credit reporting agencies to ensure the accuracy of the information they report. The reporting of late payments when no such late payments occurred is a significant breach of this requirement. 
3. Reporting of Charged-Off Accounts : XXXX, Equifax and XXXX has reported charged-off accounts on my credit report. According to the Internal Revenue Service ( IRS ), charged-off accounts are considered income, and they should not be reported as outstanding debts on a consumer 's credit report. This practice misrepresents my financial status and creates an inaccurate reflection of my creditworthiness. 
I have attempted to resolve these issues with XXXX, Equifax and XXXX directly, but my efforts have been unsuccessful in rectifying these violations. I am turning to the CFPB to seek assistance in resolving these matters and to ensure that my rights as a consumer under the FCRA are protected and upheld. 
I kindly request that the CFPB investigates these violations and takes appropriate action to address and rectify the inaccuracies on my credit report. I also ask that XXXX, Equifax and XXXX be held accountable for its failure to comply with federal regulations and its impact on my creditworthiness. 
Enclosed with this letter are copies of my credit reports reflecting the inaccurate information, as well as any related documentation that supports my complaint. 
I appreciate your prompt attention to this matter and look forward to your assistance in resolving these violations.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",FL,33169,,Web,2023-09-07,Closed with explanation,Yes
