7529950,2023-09-12,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to express my deep concern and dissatisfaction with TransUnion 's handling of my consumer request and their apparent disregard for federal law, specifically the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), as it pertains to my request for the removal of inaccurate accounts from my credit report.

The specific account I am referring to is as follows : ACCOUNT : XXXX XXXX XXXX - {$17000.00} - XX/XX/XXXX INQUIRY : XXXX XX/XX/XXXX I have repeatedly informed TransUnion that the information contained in this account is inaccurate. The character of the account is incomplete, and TransUnion continues to report a charter amount that is both incomplete and inaccurate. It is essential to emphasize that information on a consumer report must maintain maximum possible accuracy, as defined by federal law.

Accuracy, as per 15 USC 1681e ( b ), is explicitly defined as being "" correct in all details ; exact. '' TransUnion 's reporting of the details of this account falls short of this standard, as they are neither correct in all details nor exact in terms of the amounts reported.

Furthermore, TransUnion is mandated by law to comply with the FCRA, as stated in 15 USC 1681. One critical provision, 15 USC 1681i, requires TransUnion to notify me of the results of any reinvestigation. However, they have failed to do so despite multiple requests.

15 USC 1681i ( 6 ) Notice of results of reinvestigation ( A ) In general : A consumer reporting agency shall provide written notice to a consumer of the results of a reinvestigation under this subsection not later than 5 business days after the completion of the reinvestigation, by mail or, if authorized by the consumer for that purpose, by other means available to the agency.

As the original creditor, only I can validate this debt. I do NOT validate this debt. Therefore, the following accounts must be deleted from my consumer report immediately : I hereby request the CFPB 's intervention in this matter to ensure that TransUnion complies with federal law. I urge you to use your authority to prompt TransUnion to : Conduct a thorough reinvestigation into the accuracy of the account in question.

Provide me with written notice of the results of this reinvestigation within the stipulated time frame.

Delete the inaccurate and incomplete account information from my consumer file as required by law.

I believe that the CFPB 's involvement is essential to rectify this situation, protect my rights as a consumer, and hold TransUnion accountable for its noncompliance with the FCRA. I appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to a prompt resolution.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",GA,30058,,Web,2023-09-12,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
