7609999,2023-09-26,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Trouble with how payments are being handled,"I and my wife have Direct federal loans for graduate school with MOHELA. Earlier this month I logged in to confirm auto payment was setup and the amount was correct, and it was the same as it was when we last paid in 2020. On XX/XX/XXXX I received an email they had "" updated '' our XXXX plans. The letters in their system both show XX/XX/XXXX but if you open it, it is dated XX/XX/XXXX. They had us both set at the exact same rate which was double what it was before. Her repayment starts on XX/XX/XXXX and mine on XX/XX/XXXX. 

Upon looking into this, what happened to me ( and essentially EVERYONE in this situation, if you look on their XXXX or for example this XXXX XXXX : XXXX : XXXX ) is they processed every conversion from REPAYE to SAVE as if they were a single borrower with a family size of 1, yet used the married AGI for income. You can easily show this by entering the information in the studentloan.gov sites calculator as if you had that AGI but were single and getting the number they came up with. 

